# Methods

assertEquals -  two values match = Pass

assertFalse - the test must be invalid to pass

```java
 // Test should pass despite it having bad parameters 

numbers num = new numbers();

@Test
public void invalidNum_isEven() {
    boolean actual = num.isEven("!@");
    assertFalse(actual);   
}
```

@BeforeClass -  at the very start before every test is ran, run x code#

```java
 @BeforeClass
    public static void beforeClass() {
        System.out.println("Test: StringHelper.java");
    }

    // Output: Test: StringHelper.java


```